# FR79V: frame packing (`emit_homes.zig`, `Planner.pack`) lets call results of one size share one stack slot once a
# function's slots pass 4,096 bytes. Each function below keeps 512-byte values live across loops, both arms of an `if` and
# a `match`, later calls, field views, `mut` arguments, `own` moves, a task argument, failing calls and recursion, beside
# many short-lived ones (`acc += sumb(mk(...))`) that pack into the same slots: a wrong share prints a wrong checksum. The
# expected values are those of the compiler before packing (main 9e420786ce).
